WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.255
Week 23: Perfect Tenses and Relevant Past. report experience and recent developments connect past action to present relevance sequence prior events

2
00:00:10.255 --> 00:00:18.591
Mission brief. Deliver a status update separating completed work, recent change, and work completed before a deadline.

3
00:00:18.591 --> 00:00:28.209
Preparation. Select ten useful words, three linking expressions, and two repair phrases. Plan points rather than a memorized paragraph.

4
00:00:28.209 --> 00:00:36.224
Performance. Complete the task once for fluency, review the evidence, then repeat it for greater clarity and accuracy.

5
00:00:36.224 --> 00:00:44.965
After-action review. Record what succeeded, what blocked communication, and the single change that will matter most on the next attempt.

6
00:00:44.965 --> 00:01:14.167
Model language. Ya hemos completado la primera fase. — We have already completed the first phase. Todavía no han llegado los datos. — The data have not arrived yet. ¿Alguna vez has trabajado en Chile? — Have you ever worked in Chile? Cuando llamó, yo ya había enviado el informe. — When he or she called, I had already sent the report. La situación ha cambiado recientemente. — The situation has changed recently.

7
00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:24.321
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
